Patch 36 -- expose Wine's exact DirectSound FIR loop to a native Box86 bridge.

Guest profiling at the loaded combat route put 647/717 dsound samples in this
single resampler block.  Keep the normal implementation as valid x86 and move
only the float-output convolution behind a one-pointer job ABI.  Companion
Box86 patch 06 recognises the exact helper prologue and is independently gated
by MGS2_BOX86_NATIVE_DSOUND_FIR=1; with that variable unset this patch runs the
same C loop inside Wine.

Non-float output converters keep Wine's original callback path.  Buffer
selection, committed-buffer handling, phase advancement and every DirectSound
control remain in Wine.  The candidate DLL SHA256 is
302eff548429c6b87aed3931bb0bb1acd4c4c8a130a96ae7025612c2d7eb999c.

--- a/dlls/dsound/mixer.c
+++ b/dlls/dsound/mixer.c
